TARGET: lib/arborist/index.js
REASON: treeverse is a CJS package whose `depth` named export is not detected
by Node.js's cjs-module-lexer (the value is require('./depth.js'), which the
lexer does not statically resolve).  breadth, used by yarn-lock.js and
calc-dep-flags.js, IS detected, so only this one import needs the
default-import-then-destructure pattern.

---
SEARCH:
import { depth } from "treeverse";
REPLACE:
import treeverse from "treeverse";
const { depth } = treeverse;
